# AGENTS.md

<%= app_const_base %> is a Rails application generated from [thematrixcrop/rails-template](https://github.com/thematrixcrop/rails-template).

Rails 8, Ruby from `.ruby-version`, trilogy (MySQL), Solid Cache / Solid Queue / Solid Cable, Bootstrap, Hotwire (`turbo-rails`, `stimulus-rails`), importmap, RSpec.

## Layout

- `app/lib/` holds `AppLog` and `AppConfig`.
- `app/services/` holds business logic. Controllers stay thin.
- `app/dashboards/` + `app/controllers/admin/` if Administrate is enabled (`/admin`).
- Four databases: `primary`, `cache`, `queue`, `cable`. Solid schemas live in `db/*_schema.rb`.

## Commands

- `bin/setup` / `bin/rails db:prepare` — create and migrate all databases (MySQL `root`/`root` over `/tmp/mysql.sock` by default; set `DB_HOST` for TCP).
- `bin/dev` — web + Solid Queue (in Puma when `SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA` is set).
- `bin/rspec` — specs. `bin/rubocop`, `bin/brakeman`, `bin/bundler-audit` — checks (lefthook and `bin/ci`).
- `/jobs` — Mission Control (HTTP basic; see `.env.example`).

## Rules

- Comments: English, only when the reason is not obvious.
- Logs through `AppLog.<level>(scope, event, **fields)`. Never log tokens, cookies, Authorization, full request bodies, or personal data.
- User-facing copy goes through `t(...)`. `config/locales/en.yml` is the reference; add every new key to `zh-CN.yml` as well (`spec/i18n_spec.rb`).
- Two configuration stores. `.env` (dotenv, development and test) holds machine-specific and environment-specific values: database, `APP_HOST`, log level. `bin/setup` copies `.env.example` to `.env` when `.env` is missing. Production reads process ENV, not a file.
- Env-independent secrets and shared config go in Rails credentials (`bin/rails credentials:edit`). Layout: `config/credentials.example.yml`. Read them with `AppConfig.credential(:group, :key)`.
- A new ENV variable updates `.env.example` in the same commit. A new credential key updates `config/credentials.example.yml` in the same commit.
- Conventional Commits (`feat(jobs): retry failed webhooks`).
- Lefthook runs RuboCop on staged Ruby at pre-commit; pre-push runs Brakeman and, when the Gemfile changes, bundler-audit. Skip a hook with `LEFTHOOK=0`.

## Generators

Prefer `bin/rails generate` for migrations, models, controllers, jobs, mailers, and mailer previews. Test framework is RSpec.

This template does not manage upgrades of an existing app. Run `bundle update` and `bin/rails app:update` in this repository when you need newer gems.
